# netwatch — plain cron
#
# Install with:  crontab -e   (then paste the two lines below, paths adjusted)
#
# Empty stdout = no mail. netwatch only prints when a state *change* survives
# the debounce, so this cadence is safe with MAILTO set — you get one message
# per real event, not one per sample.
#
# MAILTO=you@example.com

# ── every 5 minutes: collect one sample ──────────────────────────────────────
*/5 * * * * /usr/bin/python3 /home/YOU/netwatch/netwatch.py --config /home/YOU/netwatch/netwatch.json

# ── optional: fetch the metrics onto disk if you have no pushgateway ─────────
# (pushgateway is the better path — see README "Prometheus")
# 2-59/5 * * * * /usr/bin/python3 /home/YOU/netwatch/netwatch.py --print-metrics > /var/lib/node_exporter/textfile/netwatch.prom
